# Everything here is either reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image or must never reach it.
# Without this file the build context is the whole workspace including node_modules, and it is
# uploaded to the daemon on EVERY build — on a small deploy VM that is a minutes-long stall
# before the first RUN even starts.

# Dependencies — reinstalled from the lockfile in the `deps` stage.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output — rebuilt in the image. A stale host `.next` copied in would be picked up by
# `next build` as an incremental cache from a DIFFERENT environment.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
build
out
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Env reaches containers through compose `env_file` at RUN time, never through an
# image layer — a baked-in .env leaks to anyone who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# The mobile apps never reach a server IMAGE — but their package.json files must stay in the
# build CONTEXT, because `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` validates the entire workspace and
# fails if a package named in the lockfile is missing. Their source is a few KB and is never
# copied into any image; only node_modules and build output are excluded, above.
.expo
**/.expo
**/android
**/ios

# Not needed to build or run.
.git
.gitignore
.github
coverage
**/test
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx

# Documentation.
docs
*.md
!apps/*/README.md
